# Drawing with LLM — Qwen-7B QLoRA Fine-Tuning

> Fine-tuning a 7B parameter LLM to generate structured SVG vector graphics from natural language prompts.

**Author:** Omkar Shashank Pathare · opathare@stevens.edu

---

## Overview

This project fine-tunes **Qwen-7B** using **QLoRA** (Quantized Low-Rank Adaptation) on a dataset of 10,000 SVG–natural language prompt pairs sourced from a Kaggle competition. The goal is to train the model to produce valid, well-structured SVG markup from free-form English descriptions of shapes and compositions.

---

## Problem Statement

Zero-shot LLMs struggle to generate syntactically valid and semantically aligned SVG code. A single misplaced character breaks the entire graphic. The challenge is teaching a language model to reason about geometric structure, coordinate systems, and SVG grammar simultaneously.

---

## Approach

### Data Pipeline
- Loaded 10,000 SVG–prompt pairs from `.csv` format
- **SVG canonicalization:** Normalized path commands, standardized coordinate formats, stripped unnecessary metadata
- **Validation:** Filtered malformed and non-renderable SVGs before training to ensure clean supervision signal

### Model & Training
- Base model: **Qwen-7B** (7 billion parameters)
- Fine-tuning method: **QLoRA** — 4-bit quantization + LoRA applied to all attention projection layers (`q_proj`, `v_proj`, `k_proj`, `o_proj`)
- Hardware: Single A100 GPU (fits in GPU memory due to 4-bit quantization)
- Framework: Hugging Face `transformers` + `peft` + `bitsandbytes`

### Evaluation
- Compared fine-tuned model against zero-shot Qwen-7B baseline on held-out test prompts
- Metrics: SVG validity rate, shape alignment score, path coherence
- Result: Fine-tuned model showed improved structural accuracy and shape-prompt alignment over baseline

---

## Results

| Metric | Zero-Shot Baseline | Fine-Tuned |
|--------|-------------------|------------|
| SVG Validity Rate | Low | Significantly improved |
| Shape-Prompt Alignment | Poor | Noticeably better |
| Path Coherence | Inconsistent | More reliable |

---

